# Flutter & Dart (AMC8)

## Style & analysis
- Follow [Effective Dart](https://dart.dev/effective-dart) and project `analysis_options.yaml` / `flutter_lints`.
- Prefer `final` for locals that are assigned once; use `const` for constructors and literals where possible.

## Widgets & UI
- Prefer small widgets over one huge `build` method; extract private `_Foo` widgets when it improves readability.
- Use `Theme.of(context)` / `ColorScheme` instead of hard-coded colors when extending the UI.
- Avoid async work directly in `build()`; use `FutureBuilder` / `StreamBuilder` or load in `initState` / controllers as appropriate.

## State & async
- Prefer `async`/`await` with explicit error handling (`try`/`catch` or `.catchError`) for I/O and network.
- Keep side effects (navigation, showing dialogs) out of pure parsing helpers where possible.

## Data & persistence
- This project uses `sqflite` and bundled assets: use transactions for multi-step writes, close resources safely, and avoid blocking the UI isolate for heavy work.

## Platform
- When changing native config, edit the matching `android/` or `ios/` files and keep platform-specific behavior documented in code comments only when non-obvious.
